{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nYou are given three positive integers x,\u2009y,\u2009n. Your task is to find the nearest fraction to fraction  whose denominator is no more than n. Formally, you should find such pair of integers a,\u2009b (1\u2009\u2264\u2009b\u2009\u2264\u2009n;\u00a00\u2009\u2264\u2009a) that the value  is as minimal as possible.If there are multiple \"nearest\" fractions, choose the one with the minimum denominator. If there are multiple \"nearest\" fractions with the minimum denominator, choose the one with the minimum numerator.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++17 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\ni64 my_gcd(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    if (b == 0) return a;\n    return my_gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\ni64 my_ceil(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    return (a + b - 1) / b;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    i64 x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    set<pair<i64, i64>> s;\n    \n    for (i64 i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        i64 mini = (x * i) / y;\n        i64 maxi = my_ceil(x * i, y);\n        \n        if ((mini + maxi) * y > 2 * x * i) {\n            i64 g = my_gcd(i, mini);\n            s.insert({i / g, mini / g});\n        } else {\n            i64 g = my_gcd(i, maxi);\n            s.insert({i / g, maxi / g});\n        }\n    }\n    \n    auto best = *s.begin();\n    \n    for (const auto& [q, p] : s) {\n        i64 curr = p * y;\n        i64 target = x * q;\n        \n        if (curr == target) {\n            best = {q, p};\n        } else if (curr > target) {\n            if (best.second * y > x * best.first) {\n                if (p * best.first < best.second * q) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            } else {\n                if (2 * x * best.first * q > y * (best.second * q + best.first * p)) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (best.second * y > x * best.first) {\n                if (2 * x * best.first * q < y * (best.second * q + best.first * p)) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            } else {\n                if (p * best.first > best.second * q) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    i64 g = my_gcd(best.first, best.second);\n    cout << best.second / g << '/' << best.first / g << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\ni64 my_gcd(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    if (b == 0) return a;\n    return my_gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    i64 x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    i64 best_a = 0, best_b = 1;\n    long double target = (long double)x / y;\n    \n    for (i64 b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n        // Find the best numerator a for this denominator b\n        i64 a = (x * b + y / 2) / y; // Round to nearest\n        \n        // Check floor and ceil\n        vector<i64> candidates = {max(0LL, a - 1), a, a + 1};\n        \n        for (i64 cand : candidates) {\n            if (cand < 0) continue;\n            \n            long double curr_val = (long double)cand / b;\n            long double diff = abs(curr_val - target);\n            \n            long double best_diff = abs((long double)best_a / best_b - target);\n            \n            if (diff < best_diff - 1e-18 || \n                (abs(diff - best_diff) < 1e-18 && b < best_b) ||\n                (abs(diff - best_diff) < 1e-18 && b == best_b && cand < best_a)) {\n                best_a = cand;\n                best_b = b;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    i64 g = my_gcd(best_a, best_b);\n    cout << best_a / g << '/' << best_b / g << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.0728830375228426e-06, -6.663577369181439e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.245195097813848e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00011467275908216834, -1.537788011773955e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.6569954823353328e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -5.757642793469131e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -4.23184028477408e-05, -0.007630605716258287, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.6491513785440475e-06, 0.0, -7.271740287251305e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.04534710943698883, 0.0, 0.0, -0.003827984444797039, -4.017272294731811e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.006016121711581945, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.5762781180892